===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A piece of [[cloth]] [[cover]]ing a [[window]], [[bed]], etc. to offer [[privacy]] and keep out [[light]].
#* {{RQ:Belloc Lowndes Lodger|I|0016
|passage=Thus the red damask '''curtains''' which now shut out the fog-laden, drizzling atmosphere of the Marylebone Road, had cost a mere song, and yet they might have been warranted to last another thirty years. A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the floor; as, again, the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1944|month=November and December|title="Duplex Roomette" Sleeping Cars|journal=Railway Magazine|page=324|text=It is realised that the old Pullman standard sleeper, with its convertible "sections", each containing upper and lower berths, and with no greater privacy at night than the '''curtains''' drawn along both sides of a middle aisle, has had its day.}}
# A similar piece of cloth that separates the [[audience]] and the [[stage]] in a [[theater]].
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=The Lisson Grove Mystery|passage=“H'm !” he said, “so, so—it is a tragedy in a prologue and three acts. I am going down this afternoon to see the '''curtain''' fall for the third time on what{{...}}will prove a good burlesque ; but it all began dramatically enough. It was last Saturday{{...}}that two boys, playing in the little spinney just outside Wembley Park Station, came across three large parcels done up in American cloth.{{nb...}}”}}
# {{lb|en|theater|by extension}} The beginning of a show; the moment the curtain rises.
#: ''He took so long to shave his head that we arrived 45 minutes after '''curtain''' and were denied late entry.''
# {{lb|en|fortifications}} The flat area of [[wall]] which connects two [[bastions]] or [[towers]]; the main area of a fortified wall.
#* {{RQ:Montaigne Florio Essayes}}, Folio Society, 2006, vol.1, p.220:
#*: Captain ''Rense'', beleagring the Citie of ''Errona'' for us,{{...}}caused a forcible mine to be wrought under a great '''curtine''' of the walles{{nb...}}.
# {{lb|en|euphemistic|also "[[final curtain]]"|sometimes in the plural}} [[death|Death]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1979|author=w:Monty Python|title=w:Always Look on the Bright Side of Life
|passage=For life is quite absurd / And death's the final word / You must always face the '''curtain''' with a bow.}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} That part of a wall of a building which is between two [[pavilion]]s, [[tower]]s, etc.
# {{lb|en|obsolete|derogatory}} A [[flag]]; an [[ensign]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 5|4|2|passage=Their ragged '''curtains''' poorly are let loose}}
# The uninterrupted stream of fluid that falls onto a moving substrate in the process of [[curtain coating]].

